# Detail pages — two-column layout & section chrome

Use when building **backend detail** screens that mirror **grouped `CrudForm`** (e.g. insurance desk: inquiry, policy, insurer).

**References:** `packages/ui/src/backend/CrudForm.tsx` (grouped layout grid), `.cursor/rules/module-backend-ui.mdc`, `.cursor/rules/form-ui-consistency.mdc`.

## Shell grid (main + sidebar)

- Match CrudForm’s two-column body: **`grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 lg:grid-cols-[7fr_3fr] lg:items-start`**.
- Put **`min-w-0`** on **each** column so wide tables / long tokens do not blow out the grid.

## Section chrome (no ad-hoc shadows)

- Bordered blocks should match **CrudForm group** styling: **`rounded-lg border bg-card px-4 py-3`** — **do not** add **`shadow-sm`** on those shells unless a spec explicitly requires elevation.
- **`LeadVisualSectionCard`** follows the same outer chrome (no shadow); the inner **dashed** preview panel is intentional and separate.

## “Basics” without an extra card

- When aligning with **inquiry / policy / insurer** details: **Basics** can be **`space-y-3`** + **`h2.text-sm.font-semibold`** + fields — **no** redundant bordered+shadow wrapper around Basics only.

## Linked record previews (policy ↔ inquiry)

- Cards such as **`LinkedPolicyPreviewCard`** and **`LinkedLeadPreviewCard`** must use **`PreviewFieldCell`** + **`PreviewFieldGrid`** from **`leadDetailPreviewUtils.tsx`** (same labels, value typography, and **`gap-x-4` / `gap-y-5`** as e.g. contact preview).
- Outer section: **`rounded-lg border bg-card px-4 py-3`**, no **`shadow-sm`**; avoid one-off **`dl`** + **`uppercase`** label stacks for the same information.

## Do not

- Use **`lg:grid-cols-2`** (50/50) for these product detail pages when the create/edit form for the same flow uses **`7fr_3fr`** — keep parity.
- Move a sidebar-only section (e.g. “Other / Pozostałe”) full-width **only** to fix a **single field** grid bug — fix **`DetailFieldsSection`** / **`gridClassName`** instead (see **`.cursor/rules/form-ui-consistency.mdc`** → Detail grids).
